(7) Determinism argument: compilers are deterministic, LLMs are not - you can't reliably verify AI code without understanding it.\",\n    \"author\": \"alainrk (author), HN community\",\n    \"source\": \"TechMedia | Hacker News\",\n    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=46923543\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-24\",\n    \"topics\": [\"AI agents\", \"frameworks\", \"code generation\", \"software architecture\", \"maintainability\"],\n    \"type\": \"discussion\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"title\": \"AI Coding Agents: Adoption Trends - The JetBrains Blog\",\n    \"description\": \"JetBrains Developer Ecosystem Survey 2026 findings on AI coding agent adoption. Key insights: (1) 90% of professional developers use AI coding agents at least weekly, with 68% using them daily. (2) Claude Code has become the most widely adopted tool at 39% of developers (up from 18% in January 2026), with 47% adoption in the US. (3) Claude Code has a 31% 'main tool' rate, indicating ~80% conversion from usage to primary tool. (4) Codex adoption grew 5x from 3% to 16%, with awareness jumping from 27% to 65%. (5) GitHub Copilot lost leadership, declining from 29% to 21% adoption. (6) Cursor declined from 18% to 12%, with significant drop in China (28% to 16%). (7) OpenCode reached 7% adoption with 42% mindshare despite no big company backing. (8) JetBrains AI adoption at 9%, with Claude Agent, Codex, GitHub Copilot, and OpenCode integrated into JetBrains IDEs.\",\n    \"author\": \"Mikhail Bogdanov, JetBrains Research\",\n    \"source\": \"TechMedia | JetBrains Blog\",\n    \"url\": \"https://blog.jetbrains.com/research/2026/08/ai-coding-agent-adoption-2026/\",\n    \"published_date\": \"2026-08-18\",\n    \"topics\": [\"AI coding agents\", \"adoption statistics\", \"developer survey\", \"Claude Code\", \"Codex\", \"GitHub Copilot\"],\n    \"type\": \"research\"\n  }\n]\n",
